    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for August 11, 2026, is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 81.88 efficiency rating makes him our primary weapon against Bailey Ober. The matchup is statistically ideal; Ober\u2019s slow delivery provides a significant boost to **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s aggressive base-running profile, and his ability to capitalize on the +19% SP skill advantage cements his status as our elite play. Similarly, **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.87) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.45) offer high-floor production against favorable southpaws. **Luis Robert Jr.** specifically benefits from a 14% platoon boost against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a strong park factor and a comfortable spot in the order to drive run production.\n\nTactically, we are leaning heavily into platoon and delivery speed advantages. **Jacob Wilson** (70.33) and **Andy Pages** (65.78) represent strong starts, with **Jacob Wilson** overcoming a neutral platoon disadvantage through sheer volume of opportunity at the #3 spot. Meanwhile, our most difficult bench decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, whose 46.31 score fell just short of the cut. While **Nasim Nunez** possesses high-end speed potential, the matchup against Shota Imanaga\u2014a pitcher who effectively suppresses stolen base opportunities\u2014negated his utility in a day where we prioritized raw efficiency. **Jackson Merrill** also missed the starting rotation despite a 39.03 projection, as his matchup against Kyle Harrison proved too daunting given his struggle against left-handed pitching.\n\nUsers should remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across our roster, as any late-breaking shifts in batting order could compress the efficiency scores of **Drake Baldwin** and **Coby Mayo**. Specifically, **Coby Mayo** (53.69) is hovering near our marginal threshold; while his exposure to the Bailey Ober matchup is advantageous, his deep spot in the order slightly limits his upside. We are prioritizing high-OBP and sprint-speed profiles today to mitigate the risk of these pending lineups and maximize our chances in the SB and Roto categories.",
